<!--
  Transformer Documentation — ArchitectureOverview
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.transformer.documentation.ArchitectureOverview
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:transformercap="org.blockml.bml.transformer.capability"
  xmlns:transformerdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.transformer.documentation"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow">

  <name>ArchitectureOverview</name>
  <type>transformerdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>Stage-based transformer process and module map</is>

  <documentation><![CDATA[
    Entry: transformercap:RunTransformation (Transformer.run). Exclusive
    worktree lock. The orchestrator sequences process steps; it does not
    implement them.

    workflow:Stage is the unit of work inside a ModelTransformation.
    Process steps (Prepare, Execute, Reflect, Persist, Finalize) are not
    the same as workflow Stages. Lifecycle packages of the
    ModelTransformation live under the library-local `_meta.transform`
    package (pending / running / succeeded / failed) and match its
    status. `_meta` is the shared metadata package for the library; it is
    created when missing. Future extensions use other packages under
    `_meta`.

    Each workflow Stage runs in its own isolated agent process. Agent
    context from a previous Stage is never reused.

    [1] Prepare Execution — transformercap:PrepareExecution
        Default: deterministic. Validate the pending contract (status=
        Pending, stages with a Task each, createdAt; no executionId or
        start/finish fields on the ModelTransformation), require a clean
        Git worktree, assign a unique executionId (type:UUID), sequence,
        startedAt, and baseCommit (HEAD),
        set status=Running, relocate to _meta.transform.running, then commit.
        When template is true, leave the pending Block in place, copy it
        (including SubBlocks / bound T), set template=false on the copy,
        rewrite local type FQNs onto the copy, and relocate that copy
        instead.
        Merge CLI --parameters JSON over pending parameters, check bound T
        (default type:EmptyStruct), and write the result onto the running copy.
        If the contract is violated or the worktree is dirty, do not start.

    Then for each workflow Stage, in order:

        Persist Stage Running — clean worktree, Stage status=Running,
        Stage baseCommit=HEAD, commit. Recovery boundary: after a crash
        it is clear which Stage started and on which commit.

        [2] Execute Task — transformercap:ExecuteTask
            Default: TransformationAgent (Claude Code at the CLI). New
            process per Stage. Receives the running execution and performs
            the Task of the currently Running Stage. May change BML model
            source. Must not write ModelTransformation metadata (including
            Stages) or files under _meta/transform/. Does not commit; model
            changes stay uncommitted until Persist. Claude default:
            Edit(**/*.bml), deny Edit(**/_meta/transform/**) and
            Edit(**/node_modules/**), Bash limited to npx blockml.

        [3] Reflect on Execution — transformercap:ReflectOnExecution
            Default: deterministic. No agent process. Must not change
            the model. Reads the Execute git trace for changedFiles.
            When the Stage's captureOutput is true, copies Execute
            agent stdout onto output. Skipped when Execute throws;
            output never decides Succeeded vs Failed.

        [4] Persist Execution — transformercap:PersistExecution
            Default: deterministic. Writes changedFiles, output, status,
            completedAt, and on failure a BML exception onto this Stage.
            Commits model changes together with the Stage terminal state.
            Must not relocate the ModelTransformation. A Failed Stage
            aborts remaining Stages.

    [5] Finalize Execution — transformercap:FinalizeExecution
        Default: deterministic. Always runs after a started execution.
        Succeeded only when every Stage succeeded: status=Succeeded,
        completedAt, relocate running to succeeded. Otherwise
        status=Failed, completedAt, relocate running to failed.
        Exception lives on the failed Stage, not on the
        ModelTransformation. Commits after the terminal relocation.

    TypeScript:
    • runtime/transformer.ts → transformercap:RunTransformation
    • pipeline/prepare.ts → transformercap:PrepareExecution
    • pipeline/execute.ts → transformercap:ExecuteTask
    • pipeline/reflect.ts → transformercap:ReflectOnExecution
    • pipeline/persist.ts → transformercap:PersistExecution
    • pipeline/finalize.ts → transformercap:FinalizeExecution
  ]]></documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="transformercap:RunTransformation" relation="Defines" />
    <see type="workflow:ModelTransformation" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="workflow:Stage" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="workflow:Task" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="type:EmptyStruct" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="type:UUID" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>

</block>
